extra={
65:('N01','Aid disbursement reconciliation','IF one donor project appears in OECD development-finance statistics and IATI with an independently confirmed project crosswalk.','THEN reconcile disbursements for the same project-year and currency basis; an unexplained material gap becomes a question for the donor, not a diversion finding.','Donor/project crosswalk, transaction-type code, fiscal/calendar period and currency conversion.','Same donor-recipient project and reporting period; freeze both release vintages.',['Project crosswalk','Original donor transaction ledger','Transaction-type and conversion dictionaries'],90,1,1,2,'A reporting disagreement about aid reaching intended recipients can matter, but no actor-level key has yet been validated.'),
67:('N02','Foreign assistance award reconciliation','IF ForeignAssistance.gov and USAspending identify the exact same assistance award and fiscal period.','THEN reconcile the reported assistance amount with actual award actions after separating allocation, obligation and disbursement.','Issuing-agency award namespace plus identifier and action dates; award labels alone are insufficient.','US federal reporting and same fiscal year; preserve amendments and agency coverage.',['Award namespace crosswalk','Assistance amount definitions','Complete action history'],88,1,1,2,'Public aid totals and recipient accountability justify a focused reconciliation; misaligned accounting stages are the first likely explanation.'),
88:('N03','Defence spending definitions bridge','IF a government makes a specific defence-spending claim and SIPRI and NATO show materially different values for its country-year.','THEN construct an explicit accounting bridge and identify any residual unsupported by the government’s cited measure.','Country code, year, currency/price base, accounting scope and release vintage.','NATO member, same completed year; avoid comparing latest estimates with final outturn.',['Original national budget/outturn','Both methodology notes','Exchange-rate and GDP vintages'],82,2,2,2,'Headline commitments can be assessed cheaply at aggregate level; different totals normally reflect definitions, not hidden funds.'),
124:('N04','Claimed law versus operative text','IF an official claims that an identified bill has enacted a specific measurable protection or spending authority.','THEN trace Congress.gov status to GovInfo’s exact enacted instrument and verify that provision, effective date and scope.','Congress plus bill type/number and official version; public-law identifier and section when applicable.','US federal legislation; same Congress and enactment/commencement dates.',['Exact public claim','Authenticated enacted text','Effective-date and amendment history'],85,2,3,2,'A claim about a major legal change can be tested with precise public identifiers; no legal conclusion without reading operative text.'),
136:('N05','Request closure label versus response','IF a particular MuckRock request is marked as fulfilled and the agency case identifier is known.','THEN inspect the actual final response and released material to determine what was supplied, withheld or referred relative to the request scope.','Request ID mapped by the actual correspondence to agency case identifier, not topic similarity.','Same agency and request lifecycle; include partial/interim and final response dates.',['Original request','All response letters and attachments','Requester status-update history'],68,1,2,2,'A misleading closure label may conceal an important information gap; it is not itself evidence of unlawful denial.'),
137:('N06','Different releases of the same document','IF CIA’s reading room and the National Security Archive preserve two copies of the same consequential original document and page.','THEN compare redactions and release histories to identify a previously hidden passage or an apparent inconsistency worth explaining.','Original document number, version, page, headers and release stamps; OCR similarity only aids discovery.','Same original document, different permitted release dates; preserve declassification chronology.',['Both page images','Release notices and exemption context','Authentication/provenance of archive copy'],92,2,2,2,'A newly readable policy passage can be important; later declassification routinely explains differences without proving improper secrecy.'),
223:('N07','Producer attribution arithmetic','IF a producer-year climate claim relies on Carbon Majors and the producer files compatible production figures.','THEN recompute the attributed quantity under the stated method and isolate an unexplained input or arithmetic discrepancy.','Dated producer-to-issuer/subsidiary crosswalk, fuel, year, units and ownership allocation.','Same global production perimeter and annual interval, preserving acquisitions/disposals.',['Original production table','Carbon Majors method/version','Fuel factors and allocation workbook'],83,1,2,2,'A major climate claim merits reproducible arithmetic; scope differences and model uncertainty prevent treating residuals as concealed emissions.'),
293:('N08','Historical board disclosure reconciliation','IF an OSC issuer-year board statistic and the issuer’s filed circular cover the same population and period.','THEN compare numerator, denominator and classification with the original disclosure and its amendments.','Verified issuer identity, reporting period and specific circular version; names alone provisional.','Historical Canadian issuer cohort only; inactive series does not describe current boards.',['Original circular and amendments','OSC extraction definitions','Board turnover dates'],61,1,1,2,'Material misreporting is checkable but likely lower consequence than public-money or safety leads; classification/extraction error is the first check.'),
300:('N09','Production claim exceeds a complete total','IF an issuer claims physical output in one province and month that exceeds the unsuppressed complete provincial total for that exact commodity measure.','THEN reconcile scope and units; a persisting impossibility warrants checking the issuer claim and statistical revision.','Province, mineral, month, physical unit and product definition; issuer operations located independently.','Canada, matched month/province; no interpolated suppressed cells or mixed annual/monthly quantities.',['Issuer physical-output footnote','Statistics Canada coverage and measure definitions','Toll-processing and purchased-feed accounting'],89,2,2,2,'This offers a sharp arithmetic bound rather than a loose correlation, but only after proving the public total covers the issuer quantity.')}
